WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.580
At a station in France,

2
00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.360
you want a ticket to Lyon.

3
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.050
You say «Je suis un billet pour Lyon».

4
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.580
You've just told the ticket
seller that you are a ticket.

5
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.090
Next, a café.

6
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:14.230
The waiter asks «Vous
êtes combien ?» One word,

7
00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.130
or a whole speech?

8
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:18.560
So what does a perfect answer to a French

9
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.370
role-play card actually sound like?

10
00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:25.990
In this mission, you'll decode a café
card with three highlighter colours.

11
00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.240
Then you'll build questions from chips,

12
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.670
including one question
asked three different ways.

13
00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:34.780
Your mission: find out what
a top answer sounds like,

14
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.280
prompt by prompt.
